From 018e6ab89bb2183307bccfe76344ea2bc7846dce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:31:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Sound: SET REALISM ENABLED/DISABLED; enable checks as a dry
 run first

The realism mode gets its own name: SET REALISM ENABLED/DISABLED switches
it (realistic timing, operator panels, configuration rules, CPU speed, and
with it the sounds); SHOW REALISM shows it.  SET SOUND ENABLED/DISABLED
stays as a synonym, so existing ini files keep working; volume, mute,
power, path and sound files stay under SET SOUND.

- scp.c: SET REALISM and SHOW REALISM; help topic SET Realism (the realism
  mode text moves there from SET Sound).
- sim_sound.c/.h: sim_realism_set and sim_realism_show; the messages name
  SET REALISM ("Realism: realistic CPU speed, ...").
- The devices' messages, help texts and comments name SET REALISM
  (PDP11 hk, rl, rp, rq, rx, ry, td, tq, ts; VAX 730/750/780/820/860
  stddev, vax730_rb, vax820_ka, the syslists, sim_timer.c, sound/*/README).

Known issues 76: SET REALISM ENABLED runs the devices' enable checks first
as a dry run (sim_sound_register_enable_check: t_stat fn (t_bool apply))
and applies them only if none refuses.  Before, a refusal by a later
check (the KLESI-B TU81 rule) left the RQ units already disabled by an
earlier one (the SDI rule), although the command failed.

Tested: VAX 8200 console tests (SET/SHOW REALISM, the synonym, errors,
help, the TU81 rule, the dry run), the SDI rule regression, VMS V4.7 on
the KDB50 with the TU81 on the KLESI-B in the realism mode (BACKUP,
restore, DIFFERENCES).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SuavtftJEqWTX7fajw6zWU
